# Turn the steering wheel to `angle` while the robot stands, without moving it.
# The target applies to standstill commands only (an exact zero twist, a
# command timeout, or a twist below the steering_hold thresholds): traction is
# zero and the wheel is turned to the target at the steering limits, overriding
# steering_hold.zero_hold_time. The first command that carries motion releases
# the target and normal control continues. The call returns at once; the
# caller watches the steering joint state for the wheel to arrive (e.g. the
# behavior tree turns the wheel straight after a spin on the spot while it
# stands anyway, so the next straight drive starts at once).
float64 angle  # [rad], |angle| <= steering.max_position
---
bool success
string message
